Surface: actual bin/fm-pr-merge.sh and unmodified gh 2.104.0, real jq, git, and local HTTPS GitHub-protocol emulator. No real GitHub account, PR, or network service used. A synthetic GH_TOKEN and isolated HOME/GH_CONFIG_DIR were supplied; the proxy never forwards requests.
Oracle: author intent requires two explicitly named FAILURE/CANCELLED waivers, exact-name-only matching, distinct missing-check semantics, attended-only operation, and unchanged head binding and refusal guards. Fixture outcomes were specified independently from the merge helper.
Before/after: base ebd520e74e04ab61fda68d20be71e9b9fa573105 executable refuses the identical pair with exit 2; current executable merges with exit 0, exactly one mutation, and the verified SHA in expectedHeadOid.
All CLI transcripts and actual local HTTP requests/responses are retained. No screenshots: this is a shell CLI, with no rendered UI.
Targeted checks: seven existing waiver-related functions passed via tests/.waiver-target.test.sh (temporary selector excluding standalone test calls). An initial selector included earlier standalone calls and timed out at 180 seconds; that incomplete invocation was not counted as a pass. Its partial output is retained in targeted-tests.log.
The emulator server was shut down and joined by the driver; commands were synchronous. All disposable working-tree scripts, fixture homes, certificates, and repositories were removed after capturing evidence. No product or test-source changes required.
